    "path": "/about",
    "source": "src/pages/About.tsx",
    "text": "About Ignite\nWhy we started and what we do.\nOur Story\n\"What do you want to be when you grow up?\"\nYou've probably been asked that since you were five. Nobody really updates the answer though. By the time you graduate college, a lot of the careers you're being pointed toward today will look different. Some might not exist the same way at all. That is not meant to scare anyone. It is just where things are heading.\nSo the question isn't what job to pick. It's whether you actually know how to communicate, how to carry yourself, how to figure out what you're good at. That's harder to teach than it sounds, and most school curriculums aren't built for it.\nIgnite is a student-led education initiative building free courses in practical life skills. Our Summer 2026 program brought students and high school mentors together. Now we’re developing live and independent learning so students can keep exploring and practicing.\nPractical skills for everyday life: managing your time, communicating clearly, staying safe online, understanding money, and turning ideas into projects.\nIgnite welcomes all students. Bring your curiosity and a willingness to learn.\nRight now, knowing yourself is more useful than knowing what job to aim for.\nOur Mission\nAccess\nWe keep Ignite free so more students can try these classes without worrying about cost.\nConnection\nWe build on student mentorship as we develop live and independent courses with practice and feedback.\nPractice\nOur course plans focus on skills students can use in daily life, from managing time and money to communication and online safety.\nWhy This Matters\nStudents everywhere ask: \"What am I good at? What could I become?\"\nMany students do not get early access to this kind of support\nTrying new skills early can make school feel less confusing\nHigh school mentors can explain things in a way younger students understand\nSmall wins help students feel more ready for what comes next"
